Provisioning u-boot variant (BROM/UART RAM boot) for openwrt-one.

A dedicated u-boot used ONLY for first install / repair via BROM + mtk_uartboot.
Unlike the production NAND u-boot (ENV_IS_IN_UBI, A/B boot, reset-button gated
usb_recover), this one is ENV_IS_NOWHERE so it NEVER reads the (stock/foreign)
NAND env and always runs its compiled provisioning env. On boot it auto-scans USB
for snand-factory.bin, CRC-verifies it, writes the whole NAND, verifies the
readback, and resets into the freshly-flashed firmware -- no button, no commands.
While no/invalid USB image is present it blinks the red LED and re-scans every few
seconds (Ctrl-C drops to the prompt; space stops the initial 3s autoboot).
make-flashkit ships this variant's fip as the BROM payload; the production u-boot
keeps going into NAND.
